cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cognitive Wiring Core (CWC): evidence-first adaptive computation"
message: "If you use this system or its evidence, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yaroslav
    family-names: Vasylenko
repository-code: "local: nanochat-cwc-baseline (fork of karpathy/nanochat)"
version: "1.1.0-5a0924c"
date-released: "2026-07-21"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A verified measurement substrate and falsification harness for causally
  validating adaptive-computation mechanisms. Contains claim-tier positives
  (a benchmark with a real oracle gap; adaptive-compute Jensen gap = P(m>K);
  end-to-end routing learnable under a binding budget) and negatives (RCFR ties
  prior art; surface-matched routing shows the route decision is the computation;
  fractal emergence unsupported), plus a unifying identifiability theory
  (V_realized = oracle_gap - route_decision_cost). Not yet a proven
  Pareto-superior architecture; no independent replication.
